== scmpc 0.5.1 ==
- scmpc logs in to Last.fm again when the first login failed, for example
  because it started before the network was up; until now nothing was
  submitted until scmpc was restarted (thanks to Simon Arlott)

== scmpc 0.5.0 ==
- builds with GCC 10 and later (-fno-common) (thanks to Jeroen Roovers)
- now requires glib >= 2.28
- Last.fm login uses HTTPS and POST; all requests go over HTTPS
- the MPD password from the config file or MPD_HOST is now sent; password
  protected servers that grant no rights to anonymous clients work (#6)
- fixed unparseable Last.fm responses, which caused duplicate scrobbles (#5)
- a song is no longer scrobbled twice after seeking, and a repeated song
  still counts as a new play
- the song playing when scmpc connects to MPD is scrobbled with its real
  start time instead of 0
- unreadable submit responses keep the queue for a retry instead of
  discarding it
- single song submissions send the track number correctly
- fixed submitting single songs containing ampersands (thanks to smattie)
- fixed crashes: queue_length = 0 (thanks to smattie), long lines in the
  cache file, Last.fm responses without the expected elements, an expired
  Last.fm session, -f, --kill without a pid file, and missing replies from
  MPD
- the cache file is saved atomically
- fatal errors are logged again; the "error" log level and the default now
  include critical messages, and errors are also printed to stderr when
  logging to a file
- the daemon detaches from the terminal, changes to / and closes stdio;
  relative paths in the config file are resolved first
- SIGHUP saves the queue and exits
- the daemon refuses to start if it cannot read its pid file
- reconnecting to MPD no longer multiplies the reconnect attempts
- the removed mpd "interval" option is still accepted, with a note
- unit tests (make check) and continuous integration on GitHub

== scmpc 0.4.1 ==
- fixed segfault when connecting with a wrong password
- fixed invalid signatures on tracks with non-integer track numbers in now playing notifications
- fixed segfault on 32bit systems when submitting queue
- lowered libmpdclient dependency to 2.3

== scmpc 0.4.0 ==
- port to libmpdclient
- support for the Last.fm protocol v2.0
- config: mpd -> interval was removed
- fixed a bug that prevents loading config files specific on the command-line when no other files are found (thanks to Yann Ormanns)

== scmpc 0.3.0 ==
- Last.fm Now Playing support
- UNIX domain socket support (mpd 0.14)
- a lot of code cleanup
- mpd idle support (mpd 0.14)
- respect MPD_PORT/MPD_HOST from environment
- support for the Last.fm submission protocol v1.2.1
- new command line option: -k/--kill - kill the running scmpc
